Z||000007||btoth||10-03-2001||05:19 PM||||First, do you have the diagram?<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.bw.edu/~btoth/me/btoth-vac-dia(small).jpg">  <BR>(It's best to look at this thing upside down.)<P><BR>On this picture, there should be a rubber connector where the yellow is that holds right-corner ones together. (Mine tore and I just took it off.) The two hoses (red arrow) each have a different size, one is bigger than the other, not by much, but noticable.  The one with the red arrow pointed directly at it is connected to the top metal line (green arrow - I like arrows) on the trunk wall (if that helps sort them apart).<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.bw.edu/~btoth/me/btoth_othervac(small)-more.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dan87GT||10-03-2001||05:24 PM||||I am ok on those two lines, if you look at the bottom of your yellow drawn circle it is on one of the two lines I am talking about that plug into the EGR selenoid. Those are the two I am concerned about.||||reg||1
